---
title: ':bread: Amish Cinnamon Bread'
source: https://youtu.be/WlGyWl8C830
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 1 hour 10 minutes
total time: 2 hours 25 minutes
tags:
  - americas-test-kitchen
  - bread
  - cinnamon
  - quick-bread
  - sourdough
servings: 16
---

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F.

In a #large bowl{}, #whisk{} together @all-purpose flour{3.75%cups}, @granulated sugar{3%cups}, @ground cinnamon{1%Tbsp}, @baking powder{1.5%tsp}, @baking soda{0.75%tsp}, and @salt{0.75%tsp}.

In a #medium bowl{}, lightly beat @large eggs{3}. Whisk in @whole milk{1.75%cups}, @vegetable oil{1.33%cups}, and @vanilla extract{2%tsp} until combined.

Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and stir gently until just combined, scraping the bottom of the bowl. A few streaks or small lumps are fine; do not overmix. Set the batter aside briefly while preparing the pans.

Using a #pastry brush{}, brush the bottoms and sides of two 8.5 x 4.5-inch #loaf pans{2} evenly with @vegetable oil{2%tsp} (about 1 tsp per pan). Do not use vegetable oil spray, as the loaves will stick.

In a #small bowl{}, stir together @granulated sugar{0.5%cup} and @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}. Add 2 Tbsp of the cinnamon-sugar mixture to each greased pan, tilting and tapping to coat the bottoms and sides evenly. Reserve the remaining mixture.

Divide the batter evenly between the two prepared loaf pans. Sprinkle the remaining cinnamon-sugar mixture (about 2 Tbsp per loaf) evenly over the tops.

Bake at 325°F for 65 to ~{70%minutes}, until a #paring knife{} inserted into the center of each loaf comes out mostly clean with just a crumb or two.

Transfer the pans to a #wire rack{} and let the loaves cool in the pans for at least ~{1%hour} so the crust sets and pulls slightly away from the edges.

Run a paring knife tightly along the sides of each pan to release the bread, gently tilt each loaf out, and turn right-side up. Slice with a #serrated knife{} to preserve the crunchy cinnamon-sugar crust.
